//
// The window's body (RFC-0084; design artifacts `AppWindow`): sidebarLeft ·
// contentArea · sidebarRight under the title chrome, inset 0 8 8 from the
// window edge and 8 apart (the panes' radius 16 is then concentric with the
// window's 24). The sidebar and the properties pane are `sidebarWidth` /
// `propsWidth` px wide (240 each when omitted); the content takes the rest.
//
// THE POINT OF THIS COMPONENT is what it does NOT paint inline. Every region
// is a transparent container; the APP writes its surface in the slot body —
// as a rule one `WinPane` per region:
//
//     contentArea { WinPane { title: "", showHeader: true, … } { header { … } body { … } } }
//
// The design's default is a bare sidebar on the window glass (`bare: true`)
// beside opaque content and properties panes; a region may also stack several
// panes (8 apart) or none (RFC-0084: the panel is a per-region decision).
//
// RESPONSIVE (RFC-0084 Phase 7), tiers 640/1024 via `device.sizeClass`, the
// design's three modes mapped onto the platform's three (desktop → wide,
// compact → regular, mobile → compact):
//   wide     sidebar and properties inline (each shown by `showSidebar` /
//            `showProps`);
//   regular  the sidebar becomes an OVERLAY (`sidebarOverlay`): top 0, left 8,
//            bottom 8, 256 wide, radius 16, padding 4; properties stay inline;
//   compact  both are overlays, flush with the body's edge: the sidebar 300
//            wide with radius 0 24 24 0, the properties 320 with radius 24 0 0
//            24 (the design's min(300, 82 %) / min(320, 86 %): a percentage of
//            the window has no DSL form, so they give way only below 300/320).
// An overlay pane is the kit's frosted overlay surface (glassOverlay, a 1 px
// glassEdge, shadow3, the lit top line) holding the slot body, over an invisible
// backdrop that closes it (`WinPaneClose`) — the content behind stays undimmed
// (the operator's call); the pane eats its own taps (`WinNoop`). A
// `WinPane` inside an overlay should be `bare` there (the overlay IS its
// surface): pass `bare: device.sizeClass != "wide"` for the sidebar,
// `bare: device.sizeClass == "compact"` for the properties pane.
//
// The parts are their own components (`WinBodyRegions`, `WinSidebarOverlay`, `WinPropsOverlay`,
// `WinAppMenuOverlay`), each slot forwarded into them (RFC-0084 amendment). A slot legally
// appears in BOTH the inline and the overlay part — rule 12 only refuses two placeholders under
// the same parent, and the tiers make them exclusive.
//
// FLOATING ACTION BAR: the `actionBar` slot (a `WinActionBar`) floats centred
// over the content region, 12 px above its bottom — 56 when `liftActionBar`
// clears a content footer. It is an out-of-flow layer without a handler of its
// own, so the content under its empty sides keeps every tap.
//
// THE WINDOW MENU (TASK-0066) is the window's, not the app's: the app chip in
// `WinTopBar` dispatches `WinMenu("app")`, and THIS component mounts the kit's
// `WinAppMenu` as an overlay under the chip whenever `$state.menu == "app"` —
// every window-kit app gets the tiling rows, fullscreen, minimize and close
// without copying the dropdown. Left edge = the chip's (12 px), top = the
// body's; the backdrop closes (`WinMenu("")`), the panel eats its taps
// (`WinNoop`). The text labels are props (a library owns no i18n).
//
// THE ⋮ APP MENU is the app's content in the kit's place: while `appMenuOpen`
// the `appMenu` slot (a `WinMenu` of width 240 and the submenus beside it) is
// anchored under the chrome's ⋮ — its right edge on the button's, 145 px from
// the window's right edge (the controls, the divider and the gaps between) —
// over a backdrop that closes it (`WinMenu("")`). An app's own menus must not
// mount a backdrop while `menu == "app"` — a later overlay would sit ABOVE the
// window menu and swallow its taps.

Component WinAppWindow {
    props: {
        showSidebar: Bool,
        showProps: Bool,
        sidebarOverlay: Bool,
        propsOverlay: Bool,
        sidebarWidth: Int,
        propsWidth: Int,
        liftActionBar: Bool,
        appMenuOpen: Bool,
        menuFullscreen: Str,
        menuMoveDevice: Str,
        menuMinimize: Str,
        menuClose: Str,
        menuMoveLabel: Str,
        menuArrangeLabel: Str,
        menuSoon: Str,
    }
    slot sidebarLeft
    slot contentArea
    slot sidebarRight
    slot actionBar
    slot appMenu
    Stack {
        WinBodyRegions {
            showSidebar: $props.showSidebar,
            showProps: $props.showProps,
            sidebarWidth: $props.sidebarWidth,
            propsWidth: $props.propsWidth,
            liftActionBar: $props.liftActionBar,
        } {
            sidebarLeft {
                Slot sidebarLeft
            }
            contentArea {
                Slot contentArea
            }
            sidebarRight {
                Slot sidebarRight
            }
            actionBar {
                Slot actionBar
            }
        }
        WinSidebarOverlay { sidebarOverlay: $props.sidebarOverlay } {
            sidebarLeft {
                Slot sidebarLeft
            }
        }
        WinPropsOverlay { propsOverlay: $props.propsOverlay } {
            sidebarRight {
                Slot sidebarRight
            }
        }
        // ── the window menu (app chip) ───────────────────────────────────
        WinAppMenuLayer {
            fullscreen: $props.menuFullscreen,
            moveDevice: $props.menuMoveDevice,
            minimize: $props.menuMinimize,
            close: $props.menuClose,
            moveLabel: $props.menuMoveLabel,
            arrangeLabel: $props.menuArrangeLabel,
            soon: $props.menuSoon,
        }
        WinAppMenuOverlay { appMenuOpen: $props.appMenuOpen } {
            appMenu {
                Slot appMenu
            }
        }
    }
    .grow(1)
}
